Add you own .bin files into this directory. These files are used to drive data to inputs/outputs.
Up to 4 ADC sources, 2 DAC sources and 1 GPIO source are accepted. 

accepted names:
adc_src_ch0.bin
adc_src_ch1.bin
adc_src_ch2.bin
adc_src_ch3.bin

dac_src_ch0.bin
dac_src_ch1.bin

gpio_src_out.bin

Standalone self-checking testbenches
------------------------------------
Some testbenches here drive a single module instead of the whole chip, so they
do not need the .bin sources above and are not part of "make sim" (which builds
the top_tb project).  Run them directly, from the repository root, after
sourcing the Vivado settings.  Each one prints SUCCESS or FAILURE on the last
line.

  xvlog -sv tbn/asg_pointer_arith_tb.sv
  xelab -debug typical --timescale 1ns/1ps asg_pointer_arith_tb -s sim
  xsim sim -runall

  xvlog -sv rtl/rtl_250/interface/axi_sys_if.sv \
            rtl/rtl_250/classic/red_pitaya_asg_ch.sv \
            tbn/asg_pointer_pair_integration_tb.sv
  xelab --timescale 1ns/1ps asg_pointer_pair_integration_tb -s sim
  xsim sim -runall

  xvlog -sv rtl/rtl/interface/sys_bus_if.sv rtl/rtl/sys_bus_cdc.sv \
            tbn/sys_bus_cdc_tb.sv
  xelab -debug typical --timescale 1ns/1ps sys_bus_cdc_tb -s sim
  xsim sim -runall

  xvlog -sv rtl/rtl/divide.v rtl/rtl/classic/rp_decim.v tbn/rp_decim_tb.sv
  xelab -debug typical --timescale 1ns/1ps rp_decim_tb -s sim
  xsim sim -runall

  xvlog -sv -d RP_DECIM_PREDECODED_MODE rtl/rtl/divide.v rtl/rtl_250/classic/rp_decim.v tbn/rp_decim_tb.sv
  xelab -debug typical --timescale 1ns/1ps rp_decim_tb -s sim
  xsim sim -runall

xsim writes its work directory into the current directory, so run these from a
scratch directory if you do not want xsim.dir next to the sources.

AXI write FIFO boundary arithmetic regression:

  xvlog -sv tbn/axi_wr_fifo_boundary_tb.sv
  xelab axi_wr_fifo_boundary_tb -s axi_wr_fifo_boundary_tb_sim
  xsim axi_wr_fifo_boundary_tb_sim -runall
